# whitewildwolf playbook

When the user message contains **whitewildwolf** (any case), treat it as a request to apply this **multi-brand publishing / services site** checklist unless they narrow scope.

## Forms & backend

- Contact / quote forms POST to a **same-origin PHP** endpoint (e.g. `sendmail.php` / `api/sendmail.php`); fix `__DIR__` / includes for both entry paths.
- **Validation**, spam basics (honeypot / rate limit if present), clear JSON or redirect responses.
- Production **env** for API base path; avoid full URL in `VITE_BASE`.

## Email

- **HTML + plain-text** parts; readable from mobile clients; brand name, reply-to, subject lines per form type.
- Central mail config; handle errors without leaking internals to the client.

## Zendesk / chat

- Load snippet **after window load + idle** (or interaction-only if PageSpeed is the priority).
- **Auto-open on load** when the client asks (desktop + mobile); otherwise defer open to protect LCP.
- **Live Chat** buttons open widget with **phone fallback** if `zE` missing.
- **SPA**: sync **title + URL** to Zendesk after route changes.

## SEO & head

- Per-route **`document.title`**, **meta description**, **canonical**, **Open Graph / Twitter** (SPA updates via a small head helper).
- **`robots.txt`** + **`sitemap.xml`**; **JSON-LD** Organization + WebSite; optional `VITE_SITE_URL` for canonical origin.
- **404**: `noindex` for unknown routes; thin pages only if requested.

## Performance (baseline)

- Hero LCP image: **`fetchPriority="high"`**, **`decoding="async"`**, intrinsic **width/height** where applicable.
- **Cache-Control** for static assets (Apache `.htaccess` or host equivalent).
- Heavy third-party (chat, fonts): defer / subset / self-host when scores matter.

## UX polish

- Mobile **sticky call** tab (portal to `body`), accessible label, **motion-reduce** respected for animations.
- Match existing **Tailwind / component** patterns; minimal diffs per task.

## Inquiry admin dashboard (reusable pattern)

- Build a protected admin flow with:
  - list route: `/inquiry-details`
  - detail route: `/inquiry-details/:id`
  - PHP API route: `api/inquiry-details.php` with `action=login|logout|session|list|detail`
- Keep login credentials as **hashes only** in `includes/inquiry-admin-auth.php` and verify with `password_verify`.
- Provide hash regeneration commands in comments:
  - `php -r "echo password_hash(strtolower(trim('your-new-email@example.com')), PASSWORD_DEFAULT), PHP_EOL;"`
  - `php -r "echo password_hash('YourNewStrongPassword', PASSWORD_DEFAULT), PHP_EOL;"`
- Use session auth for dashboard access; block list/detail actions unless logged in.
- Dashboard list UX defaults:
  - table with `name/email/phone/source/created_at`
  - **View Details** opens dedicated detail page route
  - email/phone clickable (`mailto:` / `tel:`)
  - pagination at **50 records per page**
  - preserve selected page via URL query (`?page=N`) so refresh keeps page
  - add top + bottom pagination controls
- Provide polished loading states (animated loader card) on both list and detail pages.
- On inquiry routes, hide non-admin floating widgets/badges (Zendesk launcher and sticky review/call widgets) unless explicitly requested.

Copy this file into **new brand repos** or merge into global Cursor user rules so **whitewildwolf** keeps the same meaning everywhere.
